(1. Objectives and Overview) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10.5 Tf
0 0 0 rg
54 580 Td
(The main objective of this assignment is to understand and practically implement the) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10.5 Tf
0 0 0 rg
54 566 Td
(foundational pillars of distributed computing: fault tolerance, data replication,) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10.5 Tf
0 0 0 rg
54 552 Td
(and linearizable consistency. In a real-world distributed environment, servers crash) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10.5 Tf
0 0 0 rg
54 538 Td
(unexpectedly, networks drop packets or suffer high latency, and network partitions) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10.5 Tf
0 0 0 rg
54 524 Td
(divide clusters into isolated groups.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10.5 Tf
0 0 0 rg
54 506 Td
(To solve these challenges in a disciplined manner, I implemented a distributed) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10.5 Tf
0 0 0 rg
54 492 Td
(key-value storage service backed by the Raft consensus protocol, modeled according) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10.5 Tf
0 0 0 rg
54 478 Td
(to the MIT 6.824 distributed systems syllabus. The service guarantees that client) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10.5 Tf
0 0 0 rg
54 464 Td
(read and write operations remain correct and consistent even when machines fail or) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10.5 Tf
0 0 0 rg
54 450 Td
(network links get cut.) Tj
ET
BT
/F2 11 Tf
0 0 0 rg
54 428 Td
(Key Concepts Addressed:) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
0 0 0 rg
62 413 Td
(-  Fault Tolerance: The cluster automatically detects node failures through) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
0 0 0 rg
62 400 Td
(   randomized heartbeat timers \(150ms-300ms\) and initiates election of a) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
0 0 0 rg
62 387 Td
(   replacement leader without human intervention. The service remains fully) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
0 0 0 rg
62 374 Td
(   operational as long as a majority quorum of nodes is online.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
0 0 0 rg
62 358 Td
(-  Replication: State Machine Replication \(SMR\) ensures that every write command) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
0 0 0 rg
62 345 Td
(   \(PUT or APPEND\) is logged and replicated across majority nodes before being) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
0 0 0 rg
62 332 Td
(   committed. Committed entries are applied to local state machines in identical) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
0 0 0 rg
62 319 Td
(   order.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
0 0 0 rg
62 303 Td
(-  Linearizable Consistency: Every read \(GET\) and write \(PUT, APPEND\) is) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
0 0 0 rg
62 290 Td
(   sequentially ordered. The system implements unique client identifiers and) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
0 0 0 rg
62 277 Td
(   sequence numbers to ensure exactly-once semantics, ignoring duplicate network) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
0 0 0 rg
62 264 Td
(   re-transmissions.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
0 0 0 rg
62 248 Td
(-  Split-Brain Prevention: Quorum voting \(floor\(N/2\) + 1\) prevents two separate) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
0 0 0 rg
62 235 Td
(   leaders from committing conflicting values in a partitioned network.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
0 0 0 rg
62 219 Td
(-  Log Compaction & Snapshots: Periodic snapshots prevent log memory explosion) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
0 0 0 rg
62 206 Td
(   and allow slow followers to catch up using InstallSnapshot.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
0 0 0 rg
62 190 Td
(-  Durable Persistence: Node terms, votes, and logs are persisted to disk so) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
0 0 0 rg
62 177 Td
(   nodes recover accurately after reboots.) Tj
ET
BT
/F2 13 Tf
0 0 0 rg
54 155 Td
(2. System Architecture) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10.5 Tf
0 0 0 rg
54 137 Td
(The system is structured as a layered distributed service. At the base is the) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10.5 Tf
0 0 0 rg
54 123 Td
(network simulation and RPC layer, followed by the Raft consensus engine, the) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10.5 Tf
0 0 0 rg
54 109 Td
(key-value state machine, and the client library.) Tj
ET
BT
/F2 11 Tf
0 0 0 rg
54 87 Td
(Component Responsibilities:) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
0 0 0 rg
62 72 Td
(-  src/raft/raft.js: Implements the Raft consensus algorithm. Handles node roles) Tj
ET
