(Detailed Test Case Explanations:) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
0 0 0 rg
62 411.5 Td
(-  Test 1 \(Leader Election\): A 3-node cluster elects exactly 1 leader. When the) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
0 0 0 rg
62 398.5 Td
(   leader is abruptly crashed, the surviving followers detect missing heartbeats) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
0 0 0 rg
62 385.5 Td
(   and elect a new leader in a higher term within 300ms.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
0 0 0 rg
62 369.5 Td
(-  Test 2 \(Log Replication\): Leader replicates commands across 3 nodes. When 1) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
0 0 0 rg
62 356.5 Td
(   follower is disconnected, the leader successfully commits commands with the) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
0 0 0 rg
62 343.5 Td
(   remaining quorum \(2 out of 3\). When the crashed follower rejoins, it catches) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
0 0 0 rg
62 330.5 Td
(   up all missing entries.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
0 0 0 rg
62 314.5 Td
(-  Test 3 \(Partition & Split-Brain\): A 5-node cluster is split into minority) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
0 0 0 rg
62 301.5 Td
(   {0,1} and majority {2,3,4}. A command sent to the minority leader is NOT) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
0 0 0 rg
62 288.5 Td
(   committed because it lacks quorum. The majority elects its own leader and) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
